// A public constant that only a rule's `_restrict` formula mentions.
//
// `publicNamesReport'` (Theory/Tools/Wellformedness.hs:463-484) harvests the
// names of a rule with `universeBi`, the same whole-value traversal
// `freshNamesReport'` uses, so it reaches the `_preRestriction` formula
// (Theory/Model/Rule.hs:424) the `_restrict` construct leaves in the rule
// info (Theory/Text/Parser.hs:175-192).  `'ID'` is a literal, not a free
// variable, so the action fact `fromRuleRestriction` adds to the rule
// (Theory/Model/Restriction.hs:141-162) carries nothing and the name is
// reachable only through the rule info; it clashes with the `'id'` of the
// conclusion.
//
// `sapic_pubname_in_restrict` pins the same harvest through a rule's
// `process` attribute.  This row is the MSR shape, where the formula sits in
// the rule info instead.
//
// Mode `match`: the two engines agree on this shape.
//
// Compared slice: the wf report block.


theory S8RestrictPubName
begin

rule R:
  [ Fr(~x) ]
  --[ _restrict( not( 'ID' = 'a' ) ) ]->
  [ Out(<~x, 'id'>) ]

end
